A||N||6||DaRkLoRD||Backwards engine swap...?||||5||
Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||10-15-2000||03:03 AM||||I've heard of people putting a 2.8 into a former 4cyl Fiero... can you do the opposite of that and put a 4cyl in a V6 SE?<P>and yes, I have a valid reason.. I'm not (too) crazy.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||862M4inCA||10-15-2000||04:41 AM||||Well, I don't see why its not possible. Considering to do a V6 swap all that is necesary is the engine, ECM, wiring, and other assorted items "V6" items...I'm sure the same is true to go to a L4.||||reg||1
Z||000002||862M4inCA||10-15-2000||04:42 AM||||Well, I don't see why its not possible. Considering to do a V6 swap all that is necesary is the engine, ECM, wiring, and other assorted "V6" items...I'm sure the same is true to go to a L4.<P>P.S. Not sure about the transaxle tho.<P>Sorry about the double post.<p>[This message has been edited by 862M4inCA (edited 10-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-15-2000||11:42 AM||||I don't know why you'd do that but yes it can be done. It's the same as changing to any other motor. you need the ECM etc etc...<P>Far as I know the V6 and 4 bolt to the tranny the same. you just need the right flexplate/flywheel.<P>You'll also have to change the fuel pump.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||10-15-2000||03:15 PM||||Steve--Have you maybe found a really hot Iron Duke all ready set up with no home for a good price??  Let us know.  Enquiring minds want to know.||||reg||1
